The lookup table now stores a smaller index type. Lookup behavior is unchanged.

- **Smaller table:** `MESGS` is a compile-time enum constant. When it is below 255, each table entry is one byte instead of two, which halves the table to 64 KB and improves cache locality on lookups.
- **Same results:** an all-ones value of the chosen type still means "no message". The first match per message number still wins, so every return value is identical.
- **Same lookup path:** the access is still a single table load.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    typedef std::conditional<((int)MESGS < 255), FIT_UINT8, FIT_UINT16>::type idx_t;
    static const idx_t NONE = (idx_t)~(idx_t)0;
    static idx_t table[65536];
    static const bool initialized = []() {
        for (int k = 0; k < 65536; k++)
            table[k] = NONE;
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
        {
            FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
            if (table[n] == NONE)
                table[n] = (idx_t)i;
        }
        return true;
    }();
    (void)initialized;

    idx_t idx = table[num];
    if (idx == NONE)
        return NULL;
    return &mesgs[idx];
}
```

